  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Humanitarian Response to Multi-sectoral needs of Conflict-affected population in Shwegu Township</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspangtThe
project is designed to address emergency lifesaving humanitarian needs of 8600
people (4348 M and 4252 F) from 1763 households in 12 villages in
conflict-affected areas of Shwegu Township.ltspangt&#xa0;
lt/spangtThe project will meet the critical needs of 267 lactating mothers 11 M
and 6 F with disabilities 356 and 310 G under 5 years old 522 boys and 464
girls between 6 to 12 years old 497 boys and 453 girls between 13 to 18 years
old 2323 M and 2275 F between 19 to 50 years old 363 M and 398 F between 51
to 60 years old 287 M and 352 F over 61 years old who are now in displacement
due to the conflict. lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspangtThe
project will provide to basic food, safe refuge (temporary shelters meeting
minimum standard of safety), emergency shelter kits, emergency WASH hygiene
kits, emergency protection services and support including explosive ordnance
risk education as well as mental health and psycho-social support, support for
positive coping mechanism, nutrition for the mothers and infants, emergency
education supportslt/spangtlt/pgtltpgt





ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
